<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs mostly firmer as Dow ends 3 points higher.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs mostly firmer as Dow ends 3 points higher.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs ended mostly firmer in New York on Wednesday, as the Dow Industrials gained 3.70 points to 5,714.60.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S., Britain and Australia.</p>
<p>Company     Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$15	     +0 1/2</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$22 3/4	 +0 7/8</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$23 7/8	 +0 7/8</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$19 5/8	 -0 3/8</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$14		 nil</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$77 5/8	 +0 7/8</p>
<p>Guinness Peat  London  33 1/2		nil</p>
<p>Brierley	 London  64		    nil</p>
<p>NZ IT	    London  229		 +1 1/2</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col  London  158 1/2	   +0 1/2</p>
<p>Templeton	London  136 1/2	   +1 1/4</p>
<p>Lion	     Sydney  untraded</p>
<p>Goodman	  Sydney  A$1.32		nil</p>
<p>Macraes	  Sydney  A$3.27		+2</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
